summary:
Node.jsで動くのに，Denoで動かないJavaScriptのコードに偶然出会しました．
// example.ts
const あ・あ = "Hello, 世界!";

console.log(あ・あ);
一見なんてことはないコードですが，Denoで実行すると，次のようなエラーが出ます．
$ deno run example.ts
error: SyntaxError: Expected ',', got '&lt;lexing error: Error { error: (53..53, UnexpectedChar { c: '・' }) }&gt;'
  |
3 | cons...

summary_en:
I happened to come across some JavaScript code that works in Node.js but doesn't work in Deno.
// example.ts
const a/a = "Hello, world!";

console.log(A・A);
The code doesn't seem like much at first glance, but when I run it on Deno, I get the following error:
$ deno run example.ts
error: SyntaxError: Expected ',', got '&lt;lexing error: Error { error: (53..53, UnexpectedChar { c: '・' }) }&gt;'
  |
3 | cons...
